Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.87,0:00:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.27,0:00:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.61,0:00:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.45,0:00:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.85,0:01:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd suggest summoning a monster if\Nyou'd like to stay in the game, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.27,0:01:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I can arrange that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.05,0:01:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, I'll play five\Nfor the price of one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.59,0:01:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Goblin Attack Force!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.83,0:01:21.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, knock his ancient giant\Nright out of the ballpark, boys!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.63,0:01:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast, Slugger!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.95,0:01:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate Ordeal of a Traveler!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.59,0:01:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This card is about to make\Nthe game more interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.35,0:01:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I choose a random card from my hand and\Nyou have to guess whether it's a magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.23,0:01:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,trap, or monster card.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.83,0:01:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,If you guess incorrectly, your\Nmonster is returned to your hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.41,0:01:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess correctly and you can attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.95,0:01:46.89,Default,,0,0,0,,So what type of card do I have in my hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.85,0:01:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.33,0:01:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You've got a one in three chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.75,0:01:57.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's grandpa is beating\NJoey at his own game.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.59,0:02:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,because he knows joey's strategy\Nhe did teach him how to duel after
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.19,0:02:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,all well here it goes it's a trap
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.49,0:02:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,card or a magic card it's a monster i
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.93,0:02:13.53,Default,,0,0,0,,need more time i'm not getting any\Nyounger all right my answer is you're
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.61,0:02:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,holding a trap card service heads\Nmonster car that was my next guess
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.73,0:02:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid your goblins will have\Nto wait. Now my eyesight's not
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.15,0:02:31.74,Default,,0,0,0,,what it used to be But it looks\Nto me like you're defenseless
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.81,0:02:35.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Nigh in, my turn Sounds good to me
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.43,0:02:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, this should help A little\Nlater, that is But for now,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.07,0:02:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,ancient giant attack him directly
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.63,0:02:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.61,0:02:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, scapegoat!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.11,0:02:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate now!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.01,0:02:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.35,0:03:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm safe, so next turn I\Ncan blast you with my goblins!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.55,0:03:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,As usual, you're one step\Nbehind the rest of the class.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.51,0:03:08.53,Default,,0,0,0,,See, as long as Ordeal\Nof a Traveler's in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.81,0:03:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,you have to guess my mystery card\Nevery time you want to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.85,0:03:15.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What? No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.55,0:03:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, you want to play tough?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.29,0:03:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll play tough!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.55,0:03:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I already know one of your cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.97,0:03:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,All I have to do is get this masked\Nmisfit to play his other card.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.33,0:03:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll know it's in his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.17,0:03:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the card Ancient's Tome!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.33,0:03:39.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.31,0:03:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That means the card left\Nin his hand is a monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.93,0:03:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.87,0:03:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I assume you know that\NAncient Tome allows me to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.49,0:03:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,switch the card in my hand\Nwith a new one from my deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.69,0:03:51.52,Default,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.99,0:03:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,But I had it all figured out!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.03,0:03:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd like to think that, but\Nold Apnark was way ahead of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.63,0:04:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll switch my stone giants\Nto defense mode and end my turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.19,0:04:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Your grandfather just lost 1,000 life
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.57,0:04:14.85,Default,,0,0,0,,points for not attacking\Nwith his stone giants.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.93,0:04:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, he switched them into defense mode,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.65,0:04:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,which could cause him to\Nlose more points next turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.41,0:04:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But that doesn't make any sense!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.67,0:04:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Pops, it's\Ngo time! Let's do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.49,0:04:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.35,0:04:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I can summon my goblins again,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.59,0:04:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,but as long as he's got\Nthat trap card on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.07,0:04:36.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't attack unless I\Nguess what's in his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.55,0:04:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,And these scapegoats\Nwon't last much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.41,0:04:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, if he draws a monster\Nnext turn, I'm gonna lose the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.61,0:04:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.79,0:04:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's try this card again, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.55,0:04:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon my goblin force!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.37,0:04:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Care to attack me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.29,0:04:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Nope, I'm done.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.19,0:04:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Thought so!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.35,0:05:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess his strategy worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.25,0:05:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa Moto has Joey in\Nthe palm of his hand now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.13,0:05:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What is Grandpa's strategy anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.51,0:05:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.57,0:05:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No, but I have a feeling\NProfessor Hawkins does.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.27,0:05:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let's just hope\NJoey figures it out soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.01,0:05:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.15,0:05:23.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.75,0:05:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What time's my next appointment?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.87,0:05:27.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's at 10:30, Doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.49,0:05:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And the winner is Leon Wilson!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.19,0:05:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like a second opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.19,0:05:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm hot! I'm hotter! I'm tired!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.73,0:05:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm tireder!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.07,0:05:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not even a word!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.35,0:05:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a few more steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.19,0:05:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought this day would never come.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.11,0:05:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one that said it was\Na short stroll to Kaimoland.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.81,0:05:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That was three weeks ago!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.67,0:06:01.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Slight miscalculation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.35,0:06:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The important thing is I\Nwas able to get us here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.07,0:06:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.98,0:06:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.89,0:06:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all we have to do is figure\Nout a way to enter that tournament.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.29,0:06:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.25,0:06:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got a few ideas up my sleeve.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.33,0:06:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what worries me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.97,0:06:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, for some reason I\Nfeel like we've met before.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.91,0:06:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, I get that a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.91,0:06:22.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But enough small talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.07,0:06:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,In order to keep my\Nancient tome on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.49,0:06:28.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to send my sinister\Nserpent to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.65,0:06:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This activates my card's special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.43,0:06:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,allowing it to immediately return\Nto my hand with no questions asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.45,0:06:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,In case I'm going too quickly\Nfor you, let me simplify.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.31,0:06:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,My magic card is safe and I\Ndidn't have to give up a thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.93,0:06:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had about enough of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.85,0:06:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Sick of me already?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.05,0:06:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But I haven't even unleashed\Nmy most devastating card!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.31,0:06:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What would that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.09,0:06:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,My prized possession.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.39,0:06:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,My pride and glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.09,0:06:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The thing I've been preparing\Nfor since I played my first card.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.61,0:06:57.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.52,0:06:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.37,0:07:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Locked away in the ancient city behind me
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.85,0:07:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,lies a powerful creature\Nknown only in legend.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.09,0:07:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And I will set it free.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.27,0:07:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake me when story time's done.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.23,0:07:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Every card I've played is an element\Nneeded to let loose this beast.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.35,0:07:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Only a few steps remain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.03,0:07:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I move my two stone\Ngiants back into attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.55,0:07:27.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Every move he makes must get him\Ncloser to unlocking that door.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.85,0:07:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll activate the\Nmagic card, Ancient Key.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.95,0:07:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The ritual is almost complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.67,0:07:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll use the\Npower of my Ancient Key,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.91,0:07:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,along with my stone giants and my Ancient\NTome, in order to unlock the Ancient Gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.49,0:07:57.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What's behind that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.51,0:08:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You're about to find out as\NI complete the final step.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.89,0:08:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrifice my Ancient Gate,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.77,0:08:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,my Ancient Giant, and my Ancient Tome in\Norder to bring forth my ultimate monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.47,0:08:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.41,0:08:16.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Ancient dragon! Arise!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.77,0:08:19.27,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.43,0:08:36.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's breathtaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.57,0:08:37.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Could've fooled me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.77,0:08:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.91,0:08:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,So that's what he's\Nbeen waiting to summon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.31,0:08:43.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.05,0:08:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,For once, it looks like Joseph\NWheeler is at a loss for words.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.97,0:08:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I should enjoy this while it lasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.35,0:08:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, Yugi, your grandfather's\Nnot the only one with that card.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.93,0:08:55.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.05,0:09:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You have an ancient dragon, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.13,0:09:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.04,0:09:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,but I've never been able\Nto summon it because
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.23,0:09:06.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have all the necessary components.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.85,0:09:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.03,0:09:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,your grandfather is the only\Nduelist I know who possesses
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.45,0:09:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,all seven cards needed to call\Nforth this divine creature.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.51,0:09:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,So I hope you kids appreciate the\Nrare event you've just witnessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.47,0:09:23.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Over the past few years, we've been\Ninvolved in a friendly competition of sorts,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.03,0:09:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,both hunting down the same cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.21,0:09:30.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Until recently, each of us had in our\Npossession six of the seven cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.01,0:09:32.47,Default,,0,0,0,,But that would soon change.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.55,0:09:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, and, uh, by the way, Arthur, I\Nhave some interesting news to report.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.91,0:09:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you owe me a chocolate shake,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.97,0:09:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,cause I managed to track\Ndown the fifth card.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.31,0:09:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You did what?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.79,0:09:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can finally summon\Nthe ancient dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.95,0:09:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I must see it. Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.57,0:09:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but when?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.63,0:09:54.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you forget?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.91,0:09:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I've joined Kaiba's tournament.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.39,0:09:58.74,Default,,0,0,0,,What better way to show off my new card?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.19,0:10:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the cheeriest I'd\Nheard him in a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.95,0:10:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,It was?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.89,0:10:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, your grandfather is\Nhappiest when he's dueling.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.55,0:10:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it keeps him young.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.59,0:10:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess he's just a\Nkid at heart. Guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.97,0:10:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Just look at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.35,0:10:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,He's managed to summon a card he's\Nbeen waiting to play for years.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.87,0:10:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's about to use it to win this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.27,0:10:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You should consider it an honor to\Nbe attacked by my ancient dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.27,0:10:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You spent the entire duel\Nsetting up for one card.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.71,0:10:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ask me, that's\Na huge waste of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.83,0:10:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm disappointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.15,0:10:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You seem to have forgotten\Neverything I taught you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.01,0:10:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.92,0:10:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, suit yourself, because either\Nway, you're about to be wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.87,0:10:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Ancient dragon, destroy his goblin\Nattack force with legendary blades!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.15,0:10:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.47,0:10:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to my scapegoats?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.35,0:10:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I see my dragon's special\Nability threw you for a loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.41,0:11:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever it defeats one of\Nyour monsters in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.51,0:11:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,it also destroys every monster that's in\Ndefense mode on your side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.33,0:11:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.53,0:11:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never let you win.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.49,0:11:20.78,Default,,0,0,0,,This tournament is my chance to finally\Nmake it big and get some respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.95,0:11:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Like Yugi gets.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.05,0:11:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta be number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.59,0:11:26.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.91,0:11:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, try to lighten up a little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.41,0:11:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You're so caught up in winning the\Nduel, you forgot what's important.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.93,0:11:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You forgot to have fun. Fun?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.23,0:11:37.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This is serious, Yook. Chill out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.15,0:11:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,This tournament's no big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.09,0:11:43.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just a cheap way for Kaiba\NCorp to get some publicity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.77,0:11:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You realize I'm standing\Nright next to you, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.91,0:11:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Just be yourself out there.\NGot it? Thanks, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.95,0:11:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You kids are so supportive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.13,0:11:57.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so proud of you all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.85,0:11:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You're proud?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.39,0:12:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about, Hapnog?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.05,0:12:04.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now back to the door!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.73,0:12:09.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And from now on, you're not gonna be\Nthe only one having fun, tough guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.85,0:12:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, that's the spirit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.71,0:12:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Who cares if Hapnog is more\Nskilled than you? So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.51,0:12:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, he'll probably win, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.49,0:12:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,That's enough motivation!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.01,0:12:21.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.97,0:12:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, you wanna see some mad skills?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.21,0:12:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring it on, kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.95,0:12:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Here goes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.91,0:12:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.61,0:12:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to give my luck one more shot\Nwith a magic card called Roll of Fate!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.47,0:12:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This card allows me to draw up to six new\Ncards depending on what number I roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.95,0:12:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as long as I remove the same\Nnumber of cards from the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.15,0:12:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, legendary gambler,\Ncancel out his roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.59,0:12:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,wheeler gets a four and\Nthe freak in the mask gets
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.49,0:13:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,a three he shoots he\Nscores he draws four cards
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.41,0:13:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,that's what i call a hand\Nplease tell me you're bluffing
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.55,0:13:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,you're about to find out pal\Ni activate land star forces
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.43,0:13:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,this card lets me automatically\Nsummon every land star
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.05,0:13:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,monster i'm I'm holding it in\Nmy hand directly to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.01,0:13:23.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No questions asked!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.15,0:13:27.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And what do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.71,0:13:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I happen to have three!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.91,0:13:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll sacrifice my three Landstars!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.97,0:13:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me summon...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.77,0:13:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Guilford the Lightning!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.07,0:13:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.89,0:13:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,By sacrificing my three land stars, I\Nactivated Guilford's special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.75,0:14:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So all your monsters are Garners.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.95,0:14:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Not my dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.57,0:14:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What a remarkable display.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.79,0:14:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm just getting warmed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.11,0:14:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now attack him directly, Guilford.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.65,0:14:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have to guess\Nwhat card this is first.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.49,0:14:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been paying attention,\Nso don't be so smug.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.77,0:14:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That, sir, is a monster card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.71,0:14:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,More specifically, Sinister Serpent.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.67,0:14:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.01,0:14:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Now where was I? Aw, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.87,0:14:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Guildford attack that masked man now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.75,0:14:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,That'll do for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.25,0:14:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.87,0:14:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Your dragon's back. But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.95,0:14:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Quite simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.15,0:14:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,My ancient city is still in play.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.19,0:14:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And as long as that card\Nremains on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.39,0:14:54.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I can continue to bring my\Ndragon back from the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.63,0:14:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You might say it's indestructible.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.83,0:15:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have known a monster this\Nspecial can't be gotten rid of so easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.71,0:15:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.29,0:15:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Now make your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.65,0:15:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't mind if I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.39,0:15:10.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, ancient dragon, attack\NGilbert the Lightning.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.37,0:15:14.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Their monster's attack points are equal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.15,0:15:16.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then they'll both be wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.97,0:15:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But not for long, because\Nthat dragon comes back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.31,0:15:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man, not my Guildford!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.95,0:15:38.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only is your best card\Ngone, my best card's back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.87,0:15:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The odds are against you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.97,0:15:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That may be, but my\Ncards never let me down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.23,0:15:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Deck!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.23,0:15:53.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's rock!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.71,0:15:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll play a Magic\Ncard known as Pot of Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.23,0:16:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,So I draw two cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.61,0:16:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I just drew Giant True Name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.95,0:16:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That sends every magic\Nand trap card on both
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.51,0:16:14.67,Default,,0,0,0,,sides of the field back\Nto the player's hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.75,0:16:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,so I can use it to get\Nrid of his ancient city
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.77,0:16:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,and prevent him from\Nbringing back his dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.31,0:16:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.22,0:16:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Giant True Nate also sends my magic\Nand trap cards back to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.19,0:16:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe I'm about to say this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.23,0:16:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're thinking about it too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.21,0:16:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep your comments to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.49,0:16:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I may not have a deck full\Nof rare cards like yours,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.51,0:16:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,and I may not plan out my\Nstrategy step by step like you do,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.33,0:16:45.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But I think pretty quickly on my feet,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.11,0:16:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and I always trust my\Ninstincts no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.23,0:16:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess that's because I\Nhad some good teachers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.25,0:16:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.53,0:16:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Er, I mean, good for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.95,0:16:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I was taught to play the game with\Nheart, and above all, always have fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.63,0:17:02.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's just what I'm doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.73,0:17:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you ready, pal?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.27,0:17:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire away.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.61,0:17:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The first thing I'm gonna do is\Nactivate my premature burial magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.95,0:17:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,All I have to do is\Ngive up 800 life points
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.99,0:17:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,to bring one monster\Nback from my graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.61,0:17:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose my Goblin Attack Force.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.67,0:17:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll activate another magic\Ncard called Giant True Name.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.09,0:17:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.43,0:17:31.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all our magic and trap\Ncards return to our hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.95,0:17:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My city!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.77,0:17:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Without that, I have nothing\Nto protect my ancient dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.51,0:17:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Inconceivable! Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.37,0:17:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,If he doesn't screw this up, Joey may\Nactually have a shot at winning this duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.77,0:17:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid there's more\Nwhere that came from.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.45,0:17:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that premature burial's back in my\Nhand, I can activate it again! Oh, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.97,0:18:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That means Guilford the\NLightning comes back, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.21,0:18:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Guilford! Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.29,0:18:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Slice and dice his ancient dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.89,0:18:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wide open!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.61,0:18:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.52,0:18:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Any last requests?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.31,0:18:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Joey just win?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.23,0:18:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It would appear he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.15,0:18:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.59,0:18:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice duel, Stranger.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.43,0:18:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I just wish I knew who you were.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.97,0:18:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, you already do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.75,0:18:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hicka-boo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.19,0:18:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.23,0:18:51.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Way?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.14,0:18:52.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Pretty good disguise, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.77,0:18:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That could be my new look.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.23,0:18:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something I don't get, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.19,0:19:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Moto.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.10,0:19:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Why'd you join this\Ntournament in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.87,0:19:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be resting.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.01,0:19:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell you the truth, I was\Nhoping to duel you. Why me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.09,0:19:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I did teach you everything I know, so I\Nthought it was about time to test you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.39,0:19:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm. And?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.61,0:19:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I pass or what? Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.27,0:19:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If I had to grade your duel, you'd get...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.93,0:19:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,A+.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.61,0:19:26.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.52,0:19:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I aced the test!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.95,0:19:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess there's a\Nfirst time for everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.71,0:19:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Pinch me, because I must be dreaming.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.33,0:19:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, it's a figure speech.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.63,0:19:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What a way to kick things off.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.57,0:19:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Your grandfather dueled quite well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.05,0:19:43.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and you know what else?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.49,0:19:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I think he had more fun than anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.79,0:19:47.81,Default,,0,0,0,,So why'd you pick the name Anubis?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.97,0:19:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Grandpa's head backwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.81,0:19:52.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
